# License policy for this repository. Read by the bitnify license hooks; see
# /bitnify-standards:licensing.
#
# The default list is kept verbatim except for one removal: lgpl.
#
# psycopg2-binary is LGPL-3.0-or-later (with the OpenSSL linking exception) and
# reaches the JupyterHub singleuser image of deploy/singleuser transitively.
# analytics-operator-lib-python — a first-party SENERGY library, Apache-2.0 —
# hard-pins psycopg2-binary==2.9.11 in its install_requires, so the package
# arrives the moment the image installs Operator Lib, which is the entire purpose
# of that image. It cannot be dropped without changing Operator Lib.
#
# It is a pip-installed library imported at runtime inside a container, not
# linked into anything of ours, and it ships unmodified. No ODE code touches it:
# the Go backend talks to Postgres through pgx (MIT).
#
# Decided on 2026-08-19 rather than assumed. Revisit if Operator Lib moves to
# pg8000 (BSD-3-Clause) or asyncpg (Apache-2.0), at which point this line and the
# note in deploy/singleuser/Dockerfile both go away.
#
# Note on the regex: the hook wraps the alternation in non-alphanumeric
# boundaries, so plain `gpl` does not match inside `LGPL`. GPL and AGPL are still
# forbidden.
FORBIDDEN_LICENSES='gpl|agpl|sspl|cc-by-nc|cc-by-sa|osl|epl|mpl|cddl|bsl|elastic-license|commons-clause'
